# One line ending everywhere. The repository stores LF; Windows checkouts may
# hold CRLF locally, but what the Linux container gets is LF -- and a shell
# script or a config file with CRLF in it fails in ways that read as a bug in
# something else entirely.
* text=auto eol=lf

# WeeWX' own drivers, byte for byte. `drivers/PROVENANCE` carries a SHA-256
# for each, and a checkout that rewrote their line endings would fail that
# check on Windows and pass on Linux -- which is the sort of difference that
# takes an afternoon. Left exactly as they came.
#
# (The two entries that were here named paths from weewx-evo's own tree and
# matched nothing in this repository: this file was copied over with the
# package.)
src/weewx_evo_weewx_driver/drivers/* -text

*.sdb binary
*.png binary
